{"text": "Category C is Moderate to Profound Intellectual Disability. The educational description is: A student with intellectual functioning significantly below the mean and similarly significant limitations in at least two adaptive skill areas. Category C reflects moderate-to-profound levels of need. This description is about educational impact and the support required for meaningful participation. It should not be used as a prediction of intelligence, personality, or future potential.\n\nOur fictional student is Maya Thompson, who is in Grade 8 and uses she/her pronouns. Maya has a moderate intellectual disability. Her IEP emphasizes functional communication, practical literacy and numeracy, personal independence, community participation, and relationships. This background information matters because it connects the designation to observable access needs at school.\n\nWhen we plan for Maya, we ask three practical questions: What can the student already do? What barriers are interfering with participation or learning? And what support will remove those barriers while building independence? Those questions keep the profile individualized and useful. Planning should include the student, family, teacher, case manager, and relevant specialists.\n\nI will now hand the presentation to Presenter 2, who will begin with Maya’s strengths and communication.", "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural", "audio": "special-education-C-02.mp3", "words": [{"text": "Category", "start": 0.1, "end": 0.6875, "start_char": 0, "end_char": 8}, {"text": "C", "start": 0.7, "end": 1.1125, "start_char": 9, "end_char": 10}, {"text": "is", "start": 1.125, "end": 1.3, "start_char": 11, "end_char": 13}, {"text": "Moderate", "start": 1.3125, "end": 1.9, "start_char": 14, "end_char": 22}, {"text": "to", "start": 1.9125, "end": 2.0125, "start_char": 23, "end_char": 25}, {"text": "Profound", "start": 2.025, "end": 2.625, "start_char": 26, "end_char": 34}, {"text": "Intellectual", "start": 2.6375, "end": 3.3125, 